minus the probability that noone will. So now we must calculate the
probability of 4000 luck outs.  The probability of not getting a WoW at any
one time is 3999/4000, so the probability of lucking out 4000 times in a row
is (3999/4000)^4000 which my calculator says is 0.367833451. So therefore
the probability of at least one person getting a WoW on the first level is 1
- 0.367833451 = 0.632166548.

